This paragraph
verifies that
headings in the
slide body use the
body-heading scale
instead of the
promoted
slide-header scale.
The smallest body
heading on this
slide should still
read as a heading
and must not become
smaller than this
paragraph text.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mSparse Body[0m
  [1;32mAutofit[0m

One short paragraph
should become
comfortably large
without looking
like a marketing
splash page.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mDense Body[0m
  [1;32mAutofit[0m

This slide
intentionally
contains enough
body content to
force a smaller
body font. The
renderer should
preserve readable
spacing, keep
headings
predictable, and
avoid clipping
content in a
typical fullscreen
browser viewport.

Autofit should
treat this as
normal slide
content rather than
a failure mode. If
a slide is too
dense even at the
minimum font size,
the fallback should
be visually obvious
and still allow the
presenter to reach
all content.

The goal is to test
the everyday case
where a technical
presenter adds a
little too much
detail but still
expects the deck to
adapt gracefully on
desktop and laptop
screens.

